# .env.example - NEVER commit real keys. Copy to .env and fill.
# Use Windows Credential Manager, 1Password, Doppler, or GitHub Secrets for prod/CI.
# This file is for local dev only. Load with python-dotenv or os.getenv in setup.

OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-openai-project-key-here
XAI_API_KEY=your-xai-key-here
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-google-key-here
# Add others as needed for the 20 modules (Notion tokens etc. via secure store)

# Hygiene: this project uses workload identity where possible, env-only for long-lived keys.
# Run secret scans in CI.

# For MAXIMIZED Google Drive / OneDrive mirroring connectors (used by gpt_external_public_mapper, bulk scripts, provider_google):
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=... (secure store only, never commit)
# ONEDRIVE_CLIENT_ID=...
# ONEDRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET=... (or use token cache via secure means)